⚡️🇺🇦 Ukraine’s National Anti-Corruption Bureau has uncovered a scheme involving the theft of over $1.28 million in foreign donor funds designated for Ukrainian support.

The group was led by a former State Secretary of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. Suspects allegedly laundered the funds through conversion centres for personal gain. Those under suspicion include the ex-State Secretary of the MFA (2020–2024), identified as the alleged organizer; a former chief of staff to the State Secretary, currently an active diplomat; an adviser to a former foreign minister and head of a controlled NGO; and the NGO’s accountant.

